# Local-only secrets for `wrangler dev`. Copy to `.dev.vars` and fill in.
#
#   cp .dev.vars.example .dev.vars
#
# `.dev.vars` is gitignored and must stay that way. It is read by the Worker at
# runtime, never bundled, and never reaches the browser — the Sky panel talks
# only to /api/sky on our own origin and receives an answer plus source links.
#
# PRODUCTION DOES NOT USE THIS FILE. Set the real key as a Cloudflare secret,
# which is encrypted at rest and not visible in the dashboard afterwards:
#
#   npx wrangler secret put SKY_API_KEY
#
# Rotate it by running that again; no deploy is needed. If it ever leaks,
# revoke at the provider first and rotate second — revoking is what stops the
# spend, rotating only stops the old key being useful.

# The provider key Sky uses. Absent or empty = Sky reports itself unavailable
# rather than answering, which is the correct failure: it never invents an
# answer from retrieved passages without a model.
SKY_API_KEY=

# WHICH VENDOR the key belongs to. Required — there is no default, and it is
# never guessed from the key's prefix: guessing wrong would post your secret to
# another vendor's endpoint, which is a credential disclosure rather than a
# failed request.
#
#   anthropic  Claude — POST /v1/messages
#   openai     anything speaking the OpenAI chat-completions shape: OpenAI,
#              Groq, Together, DeepSeek, Fireworks, OpenRouter, vLLM, Ollama.
#              Set SKY_BASE_URL for anything except OpenAI itself.
SKY_PROVIDER=

# Required. Which model to call. Kept server-side with the key so the browser
# never learns it.
SKY_MODEL=

# Optional. Only for an OpenAI-compatible endpoint that is not OpenAI —
# including a model you host yourself, which matters in places where sending a
# child's question to a foreign API is a real objection. No trailing slash.
#   e.g. https://api.groq.com/openai   or   http://localhost:11434/v1
SKY_BASE_URL=

# NOTE: the daily spend ceiling is NOT here. It lives in the sky_budget table
# so the check and the increment happen in one statement under a row lock — a
# limit in a config file cannot stop two concurrent requests both passing it.
# Adjust it from /admin/sky, or in the database directly.
